  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A conveyor belt moves horizontally with a fixed speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>. Sand falls vertically onto the belt with a steady flow of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q \\text{ kg s}^{-1}\"></span>. Which pair of expressions correctly identifies the power <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> required to maintain the belt's motion and the rate <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> at which the sand gains kinetic energy?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P = Q v^2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R = \\frac{1}{2} Q v^2\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P = \\frac{1}{2} Q v^2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R = \\frac{1}{2} Q v^2\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P = Q v^2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R = Q v^2\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P = 2 Q v^2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R = Q v^2\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
